        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0117" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg27"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/951</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tanaka</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-14"><hi rendition="#italic">January 14, 1918</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 15</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Under instructions from Viscount Motono I
                    have the honor to acquaint you for your strictly confidential information that
                    the Imperial Government have recently decided upon the dispatch of two warships,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Asahi</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Iwami</hi>,
                    to Vladivostok for the purpose of affording protection in case of emergency to
                    the resident Japanese <pb facs="0118" n="28" xml:id="pg28"/> and Allied subjects
                    and citizens and that the <hi rendition="#italic">Iwami</hi> was to have arrived
                    there on the 13th instant.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. Tanaka</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
